<%- include('partials/head') %>
  <body>
<%- include('partials/nav') %>

    <main>
      <h2>Open Source Licenses</h2>

      <article>
        <h3>Why licenses matter</h3>
        <p>
          Public code isn't automatically free to use. The license is what gives you
          permission. It tells you what you can do with the code and what you have to
          do in return.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most licenses fall into two groups. Permissive licenses like MIT let you do
          almost anything, as long as you keep the original copyright notice.
          Copyleft licenses like the GPL ask that if you share a changed version, you
          share its code under the same license.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>The ones you'll see the most</h3>
        <table>
          <tr>
            <th>ID</th>
            <th>Full name</th>
            <th>OSI approved</th>
          </tr>
          <% for (let id of popular) { %>
            <tr>
              <td><%= id %></td>
              <td><a href="<%= licenses[id].url %>"><%= licenses[id].name %></a></td>
              <td><%= licenses[id].osiApproved ? "Yes" : "No" %></td>
            </tr>
          <% } %>
        </table>
      </article>

      <aside>
        <p>
          There are a lot more than six. The SPDX list has <%= total %> licenses, and
          only <%= approved %> of them are approved by the Open Source Initiative.
        </p>
      </aside>

      <section class="sources">
        <h3>Sources</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>License data from the <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/spdx-license-list">spdx-license-list</a> package</li>
          <li><a href="https://spdx.org/licenses/">SPDX License List</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://choosealicense.com/licenses/">Choose a License, Licenses</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
  </body>
</html>
